SRC/perp -- perp, as built for OS-9/68000=========================================ORIG holds the post as comp.sources.games carried it.  perp.c and perp.hdiffer from it only inside #ifdef OSK:  - the map and sprite files are /dd/GAMES/PERP/map and /dd/GAMES/PERP/spr.    spr was made from the post's spr.expand exactly as its Makefile does    (`shrink_spr < spr.expand > spr') -- measured byte for byte against the    post's own awk script.  - the status panel printed what sprintf() returns, which BSD made the    buffer; Microware's sprintf returns a count, so Moves, Score and Level    were blank.  perp_sprintf() formats the one number each call gives and    returns the buffer.  - ^C interrupts the key read, and unix.l runs the SIGINT handler only from    check_signal(), so the key loop calls it when the read fails.  Measured:    ^C clears the screen and returns to the shell.obfus.c, the post's obfuscated variant, is not built.  A saved game goes to$HOME/cod.save.